  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's perception-action cycle, separating sensor outcomes (uncontrollable) from motion commands (controllable). The specification binds each perception outcome to a unique, safe, and progress-oriented action, enforcing conservative recovery only when needed, and ensures rapid return to exploration after recovery. Helper states are used for obstacle recovery, stuck detection, and last-resort reorientation, with strict adherence to the event and state constraints.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate perception (sensor outcomes) and action (motion commands) in the plant automaton to reflect the robot's runtime semantics.",
